# dev-registry roots — TEMPLATE (committed). Copy to the private mirror:
#     cp system/references/dev-registry.roots.example local/references/dev-registry.roots
# then edit local/references/dev-registry.roots with YOUR checkout roots.
#
# One path per line. `~` and `$HOME` expand. Lines starting with `#` are ignored.
# List nested roots explicitly (the scan does not descend into `_`-prefixed dirs).
# If this file is absent, the scan falls back to the baked-in default: ~/Developer
#
# One-off override without editing this file:  DEV_ROOTS="~/a:~/b" bash …/dev-registry.scan.sh

~/Developer
# ~/Developer/_work/wrk        # e.g. client-work checkouts live nested here
